# fabric-cli image (spec 058 §11.1): the scan's only HIGH findings are Go modules
# vendored in the newest released client binaries the image copies, with the fix in
# upstream source but in no released binary on 2026-11-14:
#   Helm 3.22.1 (the newest Helm 3; the chart is tested on Helm 3): stdlib 1.26.9
#     (CVE-2026-111943) and golang.org/x/net 0.60.0 (CVE-2026-78661);
#   Docker Compose v5.7.1 (the newest release): golang.org/x/net 0.60.0 (CVE-2026-78661).
# Neither client is run by an agent. Each entry expires, so the scan fails again by then:
# bump Helm and Compose when fixed releases ship, and delete the entry.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-15
# Added 2026-11-20: Go stdlib CVE-2026-97054 (fixed in Go 1.26.11) in the docker CLI and
# Helm 3.22.1 binaries, the newest released (docker:29-cli built 2026-11-16, Helm 3.22.1
# 2026-10-16), both before Go 1.26.11 existed. It is a race in HTTP/1 *servers* using
# MaxBytesReader; both binaries are clients and serve nothing. The Fabric-built Go images
# (Node, host emitter) moved to the Go 1.26.11 builder instead of ignoring it.
CVE-2026-97054 exp:2026-12-15
